  "content": {
    "id": "p56-q5-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "5",
    "prompt": "A 20 cm piece of wire is bent to form a rectangle. Let $x$ cm be the breadth of the rectangle.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p56-q5-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Using the perimeter, explain why the length of the rectangle can be written as $10-x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$l=10-x$ cm, since $2x+2l=20$.",
          "worked": "The perimeter is 20 cm.\n$$\\begin{align*}x+x+l+l&=20\\\\2x+2l&=20\\\\2l&=20-2x\\\\l&=10-x\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q5-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Write an equation for the area of the rectangle $A$ cm² in terms of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=x(10-x)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=lx\\\\A&=x(10-x)\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q5-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Sketch the graph of $A$ vs $x$ for suitable values of $x$.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [
          {
            "id": "p56-q5-c-axes",
            "role": "question",
            "format": "tikz",
            "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"p56 p56-q5-c-axes\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=1cm,y=1cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-2.9,-2.8) rectangle (3.2,3.1);\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (-2.7,0)--(2.8,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[<->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-2.6)--(0,2.8) node[above] {$A$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
            "src": null,
            "widthMm": 80,
            "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
            "overlayOf": null,
            "transparent": false,
            "axes": null,
            "spec": {
              "sourcePage": 56,
              "sourceRegion": "Question 5c, blank axes",
              "description": "Blank perpendicular axes with arrows at both ends; no ticks, grid, origin label or completed curve. Vertical label corrected to A.",
              "mathematics": "Drawing scaffold for A=x(10-x), with suitable domain 0<x<10.",
              "answerVisibility": "Axes only are student-visible."
            },
            "derived": false,
            "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
          }
        ],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$A=-(x-5)^2+25$, for $0<x<10$: a concave-down arc with maximum at $(5,25)$ and limiting intercepts $(0,0)$ and $(10,0)$.",
          "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}A&=x(10-x)\\\\A&=-x^2+10x\\\\A&=-(x^2-10x+25)+25\\\\A&=-(x-5)^2+25\\end{align*}$$\nThe graph is concave down, with vertex $(5,25)$ and axis of symmetry $x=5$. Its intercepts are $(0,0)$ and $(10,0)$. Both dimensions must be positive, so the suitable domain is $0<x<10$; the endpoints represent degenerate rectangles.",
          "solutionDiagrams": [
            {
              "id": "p56-q5-c-solution",
              "role": "solution",
              "format": "tikz",
              "code": "% mathsmap-diagram-colours {\"version\":1,\"kind\":\"graph\",\"base\":[],\"semantic\":[],\"reference\":\"p56 p56-q5-c-solution\"}\n\\begin{tikzpicture}[x=0.48cm,y=0.13cm]\n\\special{dvisvgm:raw <metadata data-graph-strokes=\"1\"/>}\n\\path[use as bounding box] (-1.5,-7) rectangle (12.4,31);\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (-0.6,0)--(11.5,0) node[right] {$x$};\n\\draw[->,line width=0.5pt] (0,-2)--(0,29) node[above] {$A$};\n\\draw[line width=0.8pt,domain=0:10,samples=81] plot (\\x,{\\x*(10-\\x)});\n\\draw[dashed,line width=0.4pt] (5,0)--(5,25)--(0,25);\n\\fill (5,25) circle (1.3pt);\n\\draw[fill=white,line width=0.8pt] (0,0) circle (1.5pt) (10,0) circle (1.5pt);\n\\node[above] at (5,25) {$(5,25)$};\n\\node[below left] at (0,0) {$(0,0)$};\n\\node[below] at (10,0) {$(10,0)$};\n\\end{tikzpicture}",
              "src": null,
              "widthMm": 65,
              "alt": "Mathematical diagram",
              "overlayOf": null,
              "transparent": false,
              "axes": null,
              "spec": {
                "sourcePage": 56,
                "sourceRegion": "Question 5c, authored answer",
                "description": "Complete area graph, with labelled maximum and open limiting endpoints.",
                "mathematics": "A=x(10-x), 0<x<10; vertex (5,25).",
                "answerVisibility": "Answer editions only."
              },
              "derived": false,
              "reviewStatus": "needs-review"
            }
          ]
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q5-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "Use the graph to determine the maximum area that can be formed.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$25\\text{ cm}^2$.",
          "worked": "The highest point of the graph is $(5,25)$, so the maximum area is $25\\text{ cm}^2$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p56-q5-e",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "e",
        "prompt": "What will be the dimensions of the rectangle to achieve its maximum area?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$5\\text{ cm}\\times5\\text{ cm}$.",
          "worked": "The maximum occurs at $x=5$.\n$$\\begin{align*}l&=10-5\\\\l&=5\\end{align*}$$\nThe rectangle is a square measuring $5\\text{ cm}\\times5\\text{ cm}$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 16
      }
    ]
  },
